{
  "contract": "carryforward",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The generic carryforward of one savings pool (carryforwardPool) and of two pools advancing together (carryforwardPools), as pure functions over each year's own net. pools holds one or two maps from year to that year's own net; a year missing is 0. The window is targetYear − years through targetYear: a loss older than that has expired and is never seen. Each year, in order: (1) a pool's negative own net offsets the other's positive own net up to crossOffsetLimit of it (crossOffset); (2) each pool's positive remainder consumes its own pending losses, oldest year first, without limit (consumedFromCarryforward); (3) pending losses one pool still has offset what remains positive in the other, oldest year first, up to the limit left after step 1, computed over that other pool's positive own net: one limit per year and receiving pool (absorbedFromOther on the receiving pool, crossedToOther on the giving one). Only earlier years' losses are pending in step 3; the year's own negative balance becomes a pending loss after it. finalNet is the last year's balance; savingsBase adds the two pools' finalNet where positive. A cross limit of 0 is Bizkaia's (Art. 66 NF 13/2013) and keeps the pools apart; 0.25 is régimen común's (art. 49 LIRPF). A single pool is the two-pool walk with an empty second pool and a limit of 0. Amounts are decimal strings. Shared with the mobile client: both implementations must reproduce every case. expect is written by running the TypeScript core; byHand.figures, where a case has it, are worked out by hand, its arithmetic says how, and each key is a dotted path into expect.",
